From: Verm <183540171+vermingov@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:14:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] fix(linux): open middle-clicked and new-window links in
 new tabs

WebKitGTK loaded a middle- or Ctrl-clicked link in the same tab, and
"Open Link in New Window", target=_blank and window.open did nothing:
Linux views had no new-window handler.

- wry's WebKitGTK backend routes a middle or Ctrl link click to the
  new-window handler, as its macOS backend does for Command and middle
  clicks. Shift brings the tab to the front.
- Linux views get a new-window handler with the same popup rules as a
  native tab (gesture or allowed site, eight a second); it asks the shell
  for a new tab, since WebKitGTK gives a new window no view of ours.
- NewWindowRequested says whether the tab comes to the front; a
  background one goes right after its source.
- The shell tests cover WebExtensionPackageFetched again.
